Z||000002||Lurch||08-05-2001||10:14 PM||||Used grand-am seats in mine; kind of a black tweed cloth, very comfortable. I think they were out of 92-94.  Just remove grandam tracks and bolt on fiero tracks, no drilling, grinding or cussing required.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Lurch||08-05-2001||10:18 PM||||By the way , I'm 6-4, 250 lb. Your butt sits a little higher off the floor, but thats a good thing becouse you don't get pounded as hard.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||08-05-2001||10:54 PM||||Ive done this one twice, Once with Trans Am seats and once with Camaro seats....basically remove the Camaro/Firebird seat tracks and replace them with the original Fiero Tracks and your done.  <P>BTW, I am 6'3" and when I did that swap I weighed 250lbs (now down to 200) and I have no problem getting in and out of the car.<P>Search the TD&Q archive for some pics I posted.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
