Z||000010||Jonathan||08-06-2001||08:58 PM||||I have a set of 95 Grey leather seats from a Trans-am installed in my Fiero.  I almost sold them because I lost too much headroom.  As a last effort, I swapped the seat tracks out for the ones from the original seats.  As a result, I lost the rocking feature of the T/A seats.  I also had to relocate the electronics, and air compressor for the power functions.  At this time they are loose behind the seats.  I plan on mounting them to the firewall at some point.  However, I now have regained most of my lost headroom, and the seats are comfortable again.  Overall, they were a cheap leather conversion. ($100) But I am saving the originals for Mr. Mikes covers when time, and money permits.  BTW, I did not have to elongate any of the holes in the original seat tracks.  Mine dropped right in.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fierotag2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroBUZZ||08-08-2001||06:04 PM||||I have a set of 91 Honda Prelude seats.  A bit of  a tight fit but nice.<BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000012||Wannabe||08-08-2001||08:52 PM||||I'm going out on a limb on this one. I'll be picking up an almost new driver's seat from a '99 Integra. Hopefully it will fit. I need it because the movable headrest will work better with my racing harness, the lateral supposrt and comfort are excellent, and the price is right at $50CDN. The passemger seat will be removed to make room for two racing wheels and tires  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||1
